---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Capture inbound webhooks on a local port and print each event

Usage: rustman webhook listen [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --host <HOST>
          Address to bind: an IP address or localhost (default: [webhook] host in rustman.toml, else 127.0.0.1)

      --port <PORT>
          Port to bind; 0 picks a free port (default: [webhook] port in rustman.toml, else 9090)

      --allow-remote
          Allow binding an address reachable from the network

      --max-body <BYTES>
          Largest accepted request body in bytes; larger bodies get 413
          
          [default: 10485760]

      --max-captures <N>
          Exit with code 0 once N requests were captured

      --jsonl
          Print one JSON object per line per event (the banner goes to stderr)

      --workspace <DIR>
          Workspace whose webhook/mocks.yaml answers requests (default: search from the current directory upwards; none means the default reply)

      --env <NAME>
          Environment holding the signature verifiers' secrets (default: RUSTMAN_ENV, then the workspace default)

      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help
